Hi Keith,

Yes, here in the nimble manual <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-RCfunctions.html#basic-operations> we imply that  `is.na <http://is.na>` should take in an array and return an array of the same size, as you were expecting, since we indicate it
behaves like its R counterpart.

In reality it returns a scalar and behaves like `any(is.na <http://is.na>(x))`.  In looking back through our issues we have an open issue <https://github.com/nimble-dev/nimble/issues/987> to address this but have (sloppily)
never actually done so.

I'll put it on our list to try to deal with for the next release.

As a work-around, you can use `is.na <http://is.na>` element-wise as illustrated as follows.

```

is_na <- nimbleFunction(
    run = function(x = double(1)) {

        n = length(x)
        out = logical(length=n)
        returnType(logical(1))
        for(i in 1:n)
            out[i] = is.na <http://is.na>(x[i])
        return(out)
   })
c_is_na <- compileNimble(is_na)
```

